{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"898589040e8b7759","x":-300,"y":-300,"width":1104,"height":780,"type":"text","text":"### 2. P Series — \"The Playbook\" (P01–P33)\n\nThese are **ready-to-use scripts** — specific prompts you'd actually paste in to make Athena _do_ something. There are 33 of them, so I'll cluster them into logical groups:\n\n**A. Getting Athena running (P01–P04)**  \nCreate it → start it up normally → recover it after a loss → double check the recovery worked correctly.\n\n**B. Daily operations (P05–P08)**  \nProcess new info → log what changed → flag what needs leadership's attention → write the daily summary email/brief.\n\n**C. Reviews — \"checking in\" (P09–P13)**  \nDifferent lenses to check organizational health: what changed operationally, are we executing on time, are we managing well, are we strategically on track, and — critically — could we recover if something went wrong today.\n\n**D. Keeping the filing system honest (P14–P17)**  \nUpdate the HQ folders → check they're healthy/current → check different HQs aren't contradicting each other → audit the whole thing for integrity.\n\n**E. Packaging things up for backup (P18–P21)**  \nExport a snapshot of one HQ → export just the changes (a \"delta\") → export the _full_ weekly backup → validate the backup would actually work.\n\n**F. Governance checks (P22–P24)**  \nAre decisions being tracked properly? Are the historical records healthy? Are the documents/artifacts themselves still accurate and consistent?\n\n**G. Learning & self-improvement (P25–P29)**  \nCapture lessons learned → review how well Athena itself is performing → improve processes → improve the prompt playbook itself → review the whole program's direction.\n\n**H. Certification — \"does it actually work\" (P30–P33)**  \nThis is like a fire drill: check readiness → run a full recovery simulation → validate the results → formally certify it passed.\n\n**Analogy:** if M series is the employee handbook, P series is the **stack of specific task scripts** — like a call center's scripts for \"handling a refund,\" \"handling an angry customer,\" \"end of shift checklist.\""}
